WEBVTT

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:18.330
No!

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.300
No!

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:20.320
Let me go!

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.250
Let me go!

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:45.880
S-Scary...

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.350
I thought he was going to punch me.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.400
Tachiaki's pretty messed up.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:55.980
I heard he attacked someone from 
the class next door the other day.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.160
Sorry.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.080
Huh? What?

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.840
You're too heavy!

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.150
#07
Scary Dreams Are Okay 
Because I'm Not Alone

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.860
Sora-chan's late.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.450
I wonder what's wrong.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:02.800
Mii, you don't have to wait 
for Kashiwagi to start eating.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:16.380
There he is.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:21.740
That's a pretty big lunch, Kashiwagi.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.760
Does this look like lunch to you?

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.140
I shall assist you!

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.560
Thanks, Mogi-chan.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:31.230
Up we go.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:34.730
<i>How the hell are these guys so strong?</i>

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.360
Banned?

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.320
From the nurse's office?

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:39.520
Yeah.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.140
Something about the office 
equipment and damages and stuff.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.700
So they gave him sheets and a pillow.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.070
And it looked like he was just 
sleeping, so I brought him back.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:53.840
It's totally afternoon nap style.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.530
His sheets...

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.090
Oh, yeah, the other day, Suzuki said...

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.300
There's supposed to be 
an insane kid in Class 5!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:05.340
He's super bad and scary.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.040
Let's check it out.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:07.100
No.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:11.600
Apparently he lost control of himself in 
the nurse's office and got kicked out.

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:16.460
That's not him, is it?

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.810
He's having a nightmare.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:21.240
I hope he's okay.

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.240
It must be a really bad dream.

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:26.070
Get off me!

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.370
Don't come near me!

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.370
Mogi-chan!

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:40.990
Hey, are you okay?

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:41.990
Are you hurt?

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:43.290
I'm fine.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:44.340
What about you?

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.810
I'm okay.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:46.830
Thanks.

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:48.510
Mii-kun.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.650
Are you all right?

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:53.470
Mii-kun?

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:00.510
He's bleeding.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:03.720
Are you all right?

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:04.880
Back off!

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.880
Get lost!

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.160
Don't mess with me!

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.000
What is your problem?

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:18.790
Don't you have something to say 
before you go off screaming?

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:26.870
Come on, why are <i>you</i> getting so angry?

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:32.260
Damn it...

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:40.150
What's his problem?

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:49.460
<i>I just had to come, 
but I didn't know his name.</i>

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.660
<i>I wonder if he's inside.</i>

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:56.580
Perfect, I was looking for you.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:58.210
Huh? What?

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.060
His friend?

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:00.680
Is he a delinquent, too, then?

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:01.540
Scary.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.730
Don't talk to me.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:06.670
Get lost.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.800
<b>Bandage</b>

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:08.800
Here. A bandage.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:10.300
Is your hand okay?

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:14.530
Want to walk home together?

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:18.750
That way, you can say what you want without 
worrying about the people around you.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.940
Besides, you don't want to collapse again.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:27.950
Huh, you live in a condo by yourself?

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:29.210
Yeah.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:32.310
There aren't too many high 
schoolers who live alone.

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:34.490
Didn't your parents oppose?

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.500
Actually, they kicked me out.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:40.350
I have a habit of violently sleepwalking.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.210
I keep destroying things around the house.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.510
Jeez.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:48.180
Still, you just need to fix 
your sleepwalking, right?

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.590
Then you can apologize to your family, and...

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:50.640
It's not getting fixed.

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:55.210
The doctor gave up. Said they 
don't know what's causing it.

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:58.110
I only ever get nightmares in my sleep.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.600
Were you staggering earlier because 
you don't get enough sleep?

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:03.700
Yeah.

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.330
That sucks.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:08.950
It's been like this ever since 
early elementary school.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:11.700
I have protective charms everywhere.

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:14.110
You have a bunch of protective charms?

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:15.620
Y-Yeah.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:18.250
Would you mind showing me?

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:24.820
Oh, sorry, it's just that you aren't 
supposed to use too many of them.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.250
So if it's all right with you...

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:34.280
Where do you have the charms set up?

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:36.240
I think you'll know when you come inside.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:47.450
This isn't just everywhere... 
They're <i>everywhere</i>.

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:48.780
Huh?

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:54.620
Thanks, man.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:57.380
Putting them up is easy, 
but it's scary taking them down.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:00.140
Looks like you've collected all kinds.

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:04.630
I saw some that ward off baku, 
but baku eat nightmares for you.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.320
Huh, really?

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:07.610
So, here.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:13.340
A drawing of a baku?

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:16.640
Put it under your pillow at night.

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:19.920
A baku might come and eat your nightmare.

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:23.230
Then again, it's just an imaginary creature.

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:26.360
I hope so.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:31.590
Oh, yeah, I haven't told you my name yet.

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:33.960
Kashiwagi Sora.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:35.420
You can call me by my 
first name or last name.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:38.310
I'm Tachiaki Daichi.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:42.130
Call me by my last name or first name.

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:43.870
Okay, Tachiaki.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.720
My phone number.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.380
Call me if you need anything.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:49.210
I'll always be around.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:02.970
<i>Sora-kun's a good guy,</i>

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:05.810
<i>worrying about someone like me.</i>

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:12.160
<i>I want to apologize properly 
to him and everyone else</i>

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:15.940
<i>for nearly punching them.</i>

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:27.540
<i>Huh?</i>

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.640
<i>I fell asleep?</i>

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:32.550
<i>I'd normally have woken up 
with a nightmare by now.</i>

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:37.030
<i>Is that drawing actually working?</i>

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.430
Om nom nom nom...

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.440
Nom nom nom nom...

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:02.830
<i>Hello?</i>

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:03.810
Sora-kun?

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:05.360
<i>Tachiaki?</i>

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:06.090
<i>What's wrong?</i>

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:07.990
There's this weird thing in my room.

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:11.460
I think it's consuming my soul right now.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.310
What should I do?

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:20.300
<i>Eating his soul?</i>

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.220
<i>What does that even look like?</i>

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:27.130
Sora-kun!

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:38.740
It's right up in my face!

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:41.240
What are you talking about?

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.060
It's a baku!

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:47.130
It's a baku!

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:48.250
Holy crap!

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:50.000
Why isn't it running away?

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:51.030
Is it real?

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:53.650
<i>I don't know why, but he's super excited.</i>

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:52.320
Oh, man!

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:58.330
It's so fluffy and pillowy!

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.390
I-It's safe to touch?

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:01.730
It sure is.

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:02.340
See?

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:12.730
It's fluffier than I thought.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:13.480
Right?

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:16.480
Man, that's so rare, though.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:20.280
Baku are so cautious and nimble,

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:23.540
normally, they run off 
before anyone notices them.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:28.430
It must be really focused 
on eating your dreams.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:34.220
Hey, when you say baku eat dreams, 
that's a metaphor, right?

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.690
It doesn't really look like 
the tapirs at the zoo.

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:42.500
Is this your first time seeing 
these kinds of creatures?

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.040
These kinds of creatures?

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.020
This is Mii-kun the mummy.

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:50.650
Mummy?

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:51.870
Mummy.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:54.850
Creature? It's living?

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.650
But aren't mummies corpses?

00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:57.990
Well...

00:11:57.990 --> 00:11:59.990
It's a long story.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:07.320
You look pretty sleepy today.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:11.410
I was up all last night talking with Daichi.

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:14.170
Daichi? Who's that?

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:18.430
You know, the guy from Class 5 
we saw at lunch yesterday.

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:21.050
Tachiaki Daichi.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:24.310
I stopped by his place after school.

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:27.470
A baku showed up that night, so I went back,

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.560
and we stayed up talking until morning.

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:33.470
You get yourself in one mess after another.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:34.980
What's a baku like?

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:38.570
It's fluffy and pillowy.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:41.330
Fluffy and pillowy?!

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:42.820
I want to touch it!

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.390
Want to ask Daichi?

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:46.450
Yeah!

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:48.580
He's taking the day off?

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:50.480
I wonder what's wrong.

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:52.360
Let's come ask tomorrow.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:53.560
Yeah.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:02.560
I wonder what's wrong with Daichi.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:11.810
He's not here.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:14.080
Today will be the fourth day.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:15.550
I'm worried.

00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:17.690
Sora-kun.

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:19.220
Morning.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:24.950
Daichi.

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:27.430
What happened to you?

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:28.950
You were gone for three whole days.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:31.580
I was sleeping the whole time.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.840
The whole time?

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:34.880
And when I woke up, 
it was already noon today.

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:37.330
Seriously, what do you mean, "Morning"?

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:41.080
Huh, did you change your hairstyle?

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:40.840
Dude, Kashiwagi...

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:42.710
He's talking to him like it's nothing.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:42.710
Yeah, I tied it.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.200
It's not weird, is it?

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:45.720
<i>He's not the same person anymore!</i>

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.320
You think so?

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:50.970
I'm really sorry about what happened.

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:56.100
I'm sorry I didn't apologize right 
away when I punched you in my sleep.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:57.600
Oh, that?

00:13:57.930 --> 00:14:00.450
Don't worry about it.

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.670
Sora-chan told me about it.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:03.980
It must have been rough.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:07.490
I'm glad you can sleep well now.

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:10.600
Thanks for apologizing.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:13.710
<i>She's an angel!</i>

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:16.500
<i>Is probably what he thinks.</i>

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:19.600
Hey, want to have lunch with us?

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:21.110
I want to hear about the baku.

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.610
Oh, yeah, so do I.

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:24.630
I've been wondering how it's been since then.

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:26.880
You're okay having me with you guys?

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.130
Of course.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:28.830
Right?

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:31.390
Sure.

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:38.140
<i>So how did this happen?</i>

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:41.270
<i>S-Scary...</i>

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.280
What is your problem?

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:47.060
Don't you have something to say 
before you go off screaming?

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.490
<i>He was super pissed.</i>

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.910
<i>This guy's intimidating as 
hell, just sitting there.</i>

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:59.830
S-So... Where're the other two?

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:02.560
Buying some stuff before they come.

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.670
I see...

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:08.670
Do you think it's okay leaving 
those two by themselves?

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.030
Tazuki and Daichi?

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:14.680
Tazuki just gets really cautious 
when he gets involved with people.

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:18.700
I'm sure he'll be okay with 
Daichi, once they hit it off.

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:19.690
Okay.

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:24.110
Uh...

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:25.120
Yes, sir!

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:27.710
What's your name again?

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:29.550
Tachiaki.

00:15:29.550 --> 00:15:30.950
Tachiaki Daichi.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:33.950
How's your health?

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:35.680
Something about nightmares?

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:37.380
Totally fine, now.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:38.610
Thank you.

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:39.780
I sleep very well.

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:42.710
I see. That's good.

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:48.420
So... Kamiya-san, do you have any h-hobbies?

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:49.160
Huh?

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.720
I dabble in movie watching.

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:54.720
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:59.850
Sorry we're late.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:02.730
Welcome back.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.350
Sorry we're late, Mii-kun.

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:06.230
What?

00:16:12.640 --> 00:16:15.120
We can play after lunch.

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:20.880
Don't bark at school.

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:23.500
What?

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:25.750
Going through your rebellious phase?

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:29.760
Could he be trying to tell 
you two to shake hands?

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:31.830
Say what?

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:33.080
That makes no sense.

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:35.730
Fine, fine.

00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:36.860
I'll do it.

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:38.120
I'll do it, so stop barking.

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:39.010
You'll get found out.

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:47.510
Are you telling us to get along?

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:03.960
That there is Mii-kun the mummy.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.120
This is Isao the dragon.

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.770
That's Conny the oni child.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.170
Oh, man.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:16.050
All these creatures I've never seen before.

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:18.180
They're all having fun.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:23.040
Give it a break, you guys.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:25.540
Let's find a game where you 
don't have to jump on it.

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:29.190
So, do you have 
a name for the baku yet?

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:35.200
Actually, I've been calling 
it "Mukumuku" for now, but...

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:36.790
<i>Why "Mukumuku"?</i>

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.450
It ended up learning that name.

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:41.490
I wanted to give it a name that 
actually sounds like a name.

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:44.740
What did you want to call it?

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:47.640
Like... Goemon.

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:49.350
<i>Sounds tough.</i>

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:50.390
Musashi.

00:17:50.390 --> 00:17:51.950
<i>Sounds tough.</i>

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:53.050
Kizaemon.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:54.470
<i>Sounds tough.</i>

00:17:57.570 --> 00:17:58.910
Mukumuku sounds good.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:00.470
Mukumuku should be fine.

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:02.660
I think Mukumuku is okay.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.220
Huh? Really?

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:17.230
Baku move faster than the speed of sound.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:18.060
Sound?!

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:34.380
Pochi, you're awake?

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:37.980
It's a huge gathering.

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:40.760
Are you taking pictures?

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:41.570
Yeah.

00:18:41.570 --> 00:18:43.560
For my Mii-kun observation notes.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.480
You're taking observation notes?

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:47.960
I record his weight, his height,

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:51.200
and how he reacts to new food.

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:52.830
Nice.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:54.730
I think I'll do that, too.

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:55.860
Me, too, then.

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:01.710
No, I'm not doing it.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:07.150
Daichi.

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:08.970
Sora-kun.

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:09.970
Morning.

00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:12.210
You managed to get up today, huh?

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:12.980
Yeah.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.020
Huh, aren't you going to class?

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:23.470
I've caused so much trouble.

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:28.350
I'm going to go apologize to the 
nurse and the other teachers first.

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.600
It's crazy.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.160
I don't get sleepy in class.

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:35.110
My head's clear.

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:38.230
I can understand what people are saying.

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:41.490
It's like the inside of 
my head's been reborn.

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:43.010
That's great.

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:44.580
It's all thanks to the baku, huh?

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:45.330
Yeah.

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:48.410
But half of it is thanks to you.

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:53.580
If you hadn't listened to what I had to say,

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.120
<b>Bandage</b>

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.630
nothing would have changed.

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:59.350
You even came over in the middle of the 
night when Mukumuku showed up, too.

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:03.950
No one's ever done something 
like that for me.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.560
I was so happy.

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:08.760
Thanks.

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:09.580
Really.

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:12.130
Come on.

00:20:12.130 --> 00:20:14.610
Don't worry about it. We're friends.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.110
Okay, see you later.

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:20.960
Yeah, later.

00:21:56.810 --> 00:21:59.420
Sora-kun, can you hear me out again, please?

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:03.670
How did Mukumuku get in your home?

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:07.040
I'm always careful to keep the doors locked.

00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:08.450
I have no idea how it got in.

00:22:08.450 --> 00:22:10.080
It's so weird.

00:22:10.650 --> 00:22:11.560
So...

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:14.140
You want me to find out tonight?

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:15.640
Yes, please.

00:22:18.930 --> 00:22:20.650
So, with that, Mukumuku,

00:22:20.910 --> 00:22:24.180
I'd like to have you stay outside for a bit.

00:22:27.380 --> 00:22:28.630
There we go.

00:22:31.480 --> 00:22:33.080
Wait, so you're sleeping there?

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:36.290
I can't let a guest sleep on the floor.

00:22:36.510 --> 00:22:38.270
That's not true.

00:22:38.270 --> 00:22:40.670
I'll sleep there, you can have the bed.

00:22:42.100 --> 00:22:44.170
Hey, I'm still talking!

00:22:46.290 --> 00:22:48.330
He falls asleep so fast.

00:22:52.360 --> 00:22:53.760
I think you should take the bed.

00:22:55.890 --> 00:22:56.850
Daichi?

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:08.120
Um...

00:23:08.120 --> 00:23:09.200
Daichi-san?

00:23:15.320 --> 00:23:18.030
Was that your doing, Mukumuku?

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:22.910
Daichi did say he has a 
habit of sleepwalking.

00:23:22.910 --> 00:23:25.250
There must be a way to know for sure.

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:29.510
Hey, Mukumuku, did you do that?

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:32.470
Can you control Daichi in his sleep?

00:23:42.160 --> 00:23:44.770
<i>Mukumuku's the one behind it!</i>

00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:55.430
I put pink bath salts in the tub, 
and Mii-kun turned light pink.

00:23:55.430 --> 00:24:00.090
He liked it, so I think I'll 
try different colors next time.

00:23:59.700 --> 00:24:04.630
Next Episode: New Places, Strange Places,
Strange Friends

00:24:00.650 --> 00:24:01.860
<i>How to Keep a Mummy</i>.

00:24:01.860 --> 00:24:03.390
See you next episode.

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:07.690
<b>See you next time!</b>
